<%# Footer for the product's own entry pages: the three sign-in screens, the landing page
    and the SSO error page. Deliberately NOT used on tenant-branded pages (estimates,
    invoices, the portal dashboard) — those belong to the contractor, and putting the
    platform vendor's marketing link under a contractor's invoice would be advertising in
    someone else's customer relationship.

    marketingUrl is an absolute URL to a different host, so no basePath and it opens in the
    same tab: someone who wants the product site is leaving the app on purpose. %>
<footer class="auth-footer">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="auth-footer__brand">
      <a href="<%= marketingUrl %>">ConnectedWorkOS</a>
      <span class="auth-footer__sep">·</span>
      <span>Every job, start to paid.</span>
    </p>
    <p class="auth-footer__meta">
      &copy; <%= new Date().getFullYear() %> Connected Home Outfitters LLC
    </p>
  </div>
</footer>
